          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "horse": "Flicka's Girl",
              "horse_id": "5776287",
              "quote": "She was super impressive first time out at Wolverhampton. I was kicking myself after Bath as I shouldn't have run her there with a penalty and the track probably didn't suit her. The form of that race is unbelievable, though, as the winner [Betty Clover] has gone on to win the Marygate and the second [Englemere] has won twice since quite comfortably. She's a very honest filly who tries very hard, and just tries to do a little too much in the first half of a race. She was very good when second in the Lily Agnes as it looked a nice race. She's owned by a local guy from Wrexham, so she'll probably be campaigned around Chester and she looks tailormade for it. Six furlongs won't be a problem and there'll be plenty more days for her. The more experience she gets, the more she'll be able to mix it on different tracks. She could be one for the St Hugh Stakes at Newbury later on and she looks capable of picking up black type. 30-05-24"
            }
          ],
